WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.702
-Thank you. Wow! This is a dream
come true for me.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.403 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I mean, especially me

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.405
because I don't even look like
I'm gonna be funny, you know?

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:05.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's my face.
it's like a little TED Talky.

00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.746
Like it looks like I'm about to
use the phrase renewable energy.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.583 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a hurdle.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people have kids,
'cause they're like,

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, if you don't,
who's gonna take care of you

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you're old?"
But there's no guarantee

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
your kids are gonna
take care of you, you know?

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
Take my parents' kid
for example.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.894 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.930
I'd be more apt to have kids if
they would take care of me now.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like,
I would adopt someone

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.434 line:92%
if they're old enough to drive.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.103
Then my friends would call me up
and be like,

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Today, little Emma
took her first steps."

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.707 line:92%
I'd be like, "Oh, really? Wow!

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.676 size:84% position:42%
Ron just dropped me off
at the airport. Yeah."

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:47.414 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:52.252 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.119 line:92%
I love my nephew so much.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
He makes me hesitant
to have kids

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause I'm afraid
I might have kids

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then they don't
measure up to him, you know?

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
I told my girlfriend that.
She goes, "That's ridiculous."

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.095 size:81% position:41%
She goes, "That's like
never getting married

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.630
because you're afraid you're
gonna meet someone better."

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:11.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "Yeah."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.305 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm dyslexic.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's tough, man, because you
don't see it coming.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.409
You know, I just arrived in the
first grade -- you have no idea.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:19.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
I arrived in the first grade.
Everyone started reading.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"Meh, I'm gonna stare out

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:24.517
the window for a decade. But,
you guys, you do your thing."

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.986 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:29.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
I found out I wasn't going to
learn how to read at 6.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:32.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's young to get bad news
about the future.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:32.859 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.028
That's like pulling a kid aside
and being like,

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.096 line:92%
"Hey, there's a good chance

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're gonna be
a degenerate gambler."

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.099 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.533 line:92%
He's like, "What are the odds?"

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:47.373 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
Third grade was tough
'cause the teacher was old,

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:52.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she learned to teach
before dyslexia was invented.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she didn't think
it was a thing.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:56.616
She thought it was something
people made up to get attention.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.318 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Like a gluten allergy.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:03.189 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
She'd make, like,
the whole class read,

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:05.892 line:92%
and then it would be my turn.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like,
"Yeah, I can't read.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's the same situation
as yesterday."

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.630 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.464 line:92%
She'd be like, "Sound it out."

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd be like,
"Nice try. That's reading."

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.301 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.369 line:92%
That is so insensitive, man.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell a dyslexic child
to sound it out?

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.273
That'd be like if someone pulled
you aside and said,

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:23.443
"Hey, I can't eat this. I'm
deathly allergic to peanuts."

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.211 line:92%
And you're like, "Chew slowly."

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
They put me in special ed.
I was in special ed.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
My mom did all my homework,
all my projects.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.391 size:88% position:44% line:92%
They still put me there.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.194 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's true.
My mom would always say to me,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
she'd say, "You know, there's
nothing to be ashamed

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
about being in special ed,"
and I'm glad she felt that way

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause technically
she was in it too.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:55.041 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:58.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am so close to my mom.
My mom had surgery last year.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:58.912 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I went to the hospital.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was so, like, upset and
nervous I immediately fainted.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:04.450
As I came to, the doctor was
panicking and said to my dad,

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Does he have
any medical conditions

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.720 size:84% position:42% line:92%
we need to know about?"

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.090 line:92%
My dad said, "He has OCD."

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:11.791 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.661 size:84% position:42%
That's not pertinent to
the situation at all.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.229 line:92%
He just started talking smack.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
The doctor's like, "Seriously,

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
is there anything
we need to know?"

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
My dad's like,
"He owes us 5 grand."

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:24.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:27.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a new girlfriend.
She's Indian.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
And sometimes
I'll tell people that,

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.843
and they're like,
"Native American or from India?"

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.445 line:92%
And I'm like, "First off, rude."

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.313 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Secondly, I will
look into that."

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:43.289 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
She has
an emotional support dog,

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:46.926 line:92%
which I have no experience with.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the first time
she cried in front of me,

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just kind of innocently
looked at the dog

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.232 line:92%
and was like, "Do you got this?"

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:56.769 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have no experience with pets
at all.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I was a kid,
I would ask for a pet,

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:04.410
and my parents would say, "Well,
what will we do when we travel?"

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.878 line:92%
Then we never went anywhere.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:06.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.147
My friend was like, "Weren't you
lonely without a dog?"

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.750
I was like, "No, I was busy
preparing for this voyage

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:15.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
the whole time."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:18.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last time I was home, just out
of the blue, my mom goes,

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We should have
gotten you a dog."

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.094 line:92%
That always hurts, right?

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're hanging out
with your parents.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:23.596 line:92%
They start brainstorming ways

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
you could have been
a better person?

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:30.903 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:33.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
Same trip, out of nowhere,
my mom goes,

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
"When we get old, I hope you
don't put us in a home."

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.745
And I was like, "Well, what will
I do when I travel?"

00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.079 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.981 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Thank you guys so much!

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.317 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:52.358 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.461 line:92%
-Phil Hanley! Phil Hanley.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:05:00.033 line:92%
